 server←{which}Run port;folder;rc;msg
⍝ Start the Exercise 1 service on localhost
⍝ which  - [optional] 'Start' (default) or 'Solution': the folder whose endpoint files are loaded
⍝ port   - the port to listen on (the README uses 8080)
⍝ server - the Jarvis server; stop it with server.Stop
⍝          ⍬ if Setup has not been run or the folder does not exist
⍝          the Jarvis server, not started, if it could not start (e.g. the port is in use): set server.Port and run server.Start
⍝ The endpoints are loaded into #.Ex1. Edit one with )ED #.Ex1.Hello and the server uses the change straight away.
⍝ The server is also kept in #.Ex1Server, so that running Run again stops it first.
⍝ Usage:
⍝      server←Run 8080
⍝      server←'Solution' Run 8080
 server←⍬
 :If 0=⎕NC'which'
     which←'Start'
 :EndIf
 :If 0=#.⎕NC'WorkshopRoot'
     ⎕←'Problem: run Setup first (see Exercises/README.md)'
     →0
 :EndIf
 folder←#.WorkshopRoot,'/Exercises/Ex1-Tools/',which
 :If ~⎕NEXISTS folder
     ⎕←'Problem: no folder "',folder,'"; use ''Start'' or ''Solution'''
     →0
 :EndIf

⍝ Stop the server from an earlier Run, if it is still running.
⍝ Two servers on the same port in one session do not report an error, and the old one would keep answering with the old code.
 :If 9=⌊#.⎕NC'Ex1Server'
 :AndIf #.Ex1Server.Running
     {}#.Ex1Server.Stop
     ⎕←'Stopped the Exercise 1 server that was already running'
 :EndIf

⍝ Load every endpoint function from the folder into a fresh #.Ex1
 #.⎕EX'Ex1'
 'Ex1'#.⎕NS''
 {}{2 #.Ex1.⎕FIX'file://',⍵}¨⊃0(⎕NINFO⍠1)folder,'/*.aplf'

 server←#.Jarvis.New''
 #.Ex1Server←server
 server.(Port CodeLocation DYALOG_JARVIS_THREAD)←port #.Ex1 'DEBUG' ⍝ DEBUG: run in the background, keep the session usable
 (rc msg)←server.Start
 :If rc≠0
     ⎕←'Problem: could not start the server: ',msg
     ⎕←'If port ',(⍕port),' is in use, try another, for example: server←Run ',⍕port+10
     →0
 :EndIf
 ⎕←'Exercise 1 service (',which,') is running: open http://localhost:',(⍕port),' in your browser'
